From: Surface RT bring-up
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] grate: allocate fragment scalars and defer colour stores

Replace the fixed two-vec4 TGSI mapping with component liveness and bounded
scalar allocation. Preserve sampled UNORM channels and selected colours as
packed FX10; keep general arithmetic FP20. Predicate results use the condition
bank. After the final texture/varying fetch, pixel row registers can hold
persistent temporaries. Reuse a dying operand only after its last scalar read,
including individual packed halves and overwritten temporary definitions.

Defer fragment outputs to virtual temporaries until the shader has consumed
all sampled channels. Early masked stores alias R2/R3 and previously corrupted
still-live sample data. Stage the final output through a batch-local GPR copy
to avoid source/destination overlap. Emit separate batches for dependent ALU
operations, retain the tested one-row allocation, and free compiler IR.

